{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"individual-sonorous-snake","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\nThe compaction sweep's log, /var/gerrit/site/.rebar/logs/compact-worker.log inside the rebar-mcp container, is not on a volume. autodeploy.sh replaces the container on every src/rebar change (2-minute timer), so the log is discarded at each deploy. The Nov 1 PST sweep's log was lost this way, which left breezelike-travelsick-moray without per-phase production timings; Gerrit 3269 (f1fe7c6f587) added those timing lines, but they survive only until the next deploy.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The compact-worker log persists across a blue-green MCP deploy (on a mounted volume or forwarded to the journal like rebar-mcp's own log), with a test or config check that guards the location.\n- [ ] docs/mcp-client-setup.md troubleshooting (or the MCP runbook) names where to read it.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] After the next deploy, the log from the previous container is still readable.\n  provenance: production-equivalent / live-call","id":"4f4d-9a7a-3b2d-4b13","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["ops-sweep"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"compact-worker.log is wiped by every MCP deploy"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793725895836000001,"uuid":"683d008d-4fa3-4681-a90e-ef90add6acf5"}